3d6 is better (measured in terms of average blows to kill)

The problem with d20 is that the final blow that kills the monster is
likely to be a massive blow and it's likely to overkill it.  The
overkill is wasted, so your average _useful_ damage output is slightly
higher with 3d6.

I ran a tests with a series of 100000 monsters of 100 hit points
each with a weapon that scored d20 versus a weapon that scored 3d6.
The 3d6 weapon required about 1% fewer total swings

  10128148    10016242
  106331877   105164189   10.49865       10.49937    

That's 10.128 megaswings with the d20 versus 10.016 megaswings with the
3d6 for a total of 106 million damage inflicted with the d20 versus 105
million damage inflicted with the 3d6.  10.499 damage per hit on
both weapons.

The d20 weapon wasted about 6 hit points per monster with overkill.
The 3d6 weapon wasted about 5 hit points per monster.

There's probably a really neat analytical formula for this that I'm
too lazy to discover.  The Monte Carlo method is so much simpler.

